Workaround: the flow codegen (labelle-gui #102) emits
`@import("components/<Name>.zig")` resolved relative to the generated
flow file's directory (scripts/flows/), so it looks for
`scripts/flows/components/<Name>.zig` instead of the project-level
`components/<Name>.zig`. The sibling `Position.zig` symlink in this
directory points back at `../../../components/Position.zig` so the
generated `tick.zig` compiles end-to-end.

Remove this directory once the codegen emits a depth-aware path
(`../../components/<Name>.zig`) or the assembler exposes `components`
as a named module. Tracked in labelle-gui follow-up.
